From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenBMC <openbmc@meta.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Jun 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] unix/configure: don't let implicit-decl errors break feature
 probes

UnZip's hand-rolled configure detects optional features with historical
"link tests" that call library functions (closedir/opendir, memset,
fchmod, ...) without including a prototype, relying on the C compiler
treating an implicit function declaration (and implicit int) as a mere
warning.

GCC >= 14 promotes -Wimplicit-function-declaration, -Wimplicit-int and
-Wint-conversion to hard errors by default. Under such a host compiler
the probe programs fail to COMPILE, so configure wrongly concludes the
features are absent and emits -DNO_DIR, -DZMEM, -DNO_ERRNO, -DNO_FCHMOD,
etc. -DNO_DIR in particular activates an AT&T-3B1-era fallback in
unix/unix.c ("typedef FILE DIR;" + custom opendir/readdir) that collides
with the system <dirent.h>, breaking the (native) build entirely.

Restore the historical behaviour by downgrading those three diagnostics
back to warnings for the compiler used by configure and the subsequent
build, so feature detection works as intended.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [legacy package, no active upstream]
---
 unix/configure | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/unix/configure b/unix/configure
index 0a4d2d0..1111111 100644
--- a/unix/configure
+++ b/unix/configure
@@ -12,6 +12,14 @@
 trap "rm -f conftest* core a.out; exit 1" 1 2 3 15
 
 CC=${1-cc}
+# OpenBMC: GCC >= 14 makes -Wimplicit-function-declaration, -Wimplicit-int and
+# -Wint-conversion errors by default. The feature probes below are historical
+# link tests that call closedir()/memset()/fchmod() etc. without a prototype;
+# under a newer host compiler they fail to COMPILE, so configure wrongly
+# concludes the features are missing and emits -DNO_DIR/-DZMEM/-DNO_ERRNO.
+# -DNO_DIR then enables a broken "typedef FILE DIR" fallback that collides
+# with <dirent.h>. Restore warning behaviour so detection works.
+CC="$CC -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration -Wno-error=implicit-int -Wno-error=int-conversion"
 CFLAGS=${2}
 CFLAGSR=${CFLAGS}
 IZ_BZIP2=${3}
